EXPERIMENT 37 – DATA-DRIVEN TESTING USING CSV DATA SET CONFIG IN APACHE JMETER
AIM
To use Apache JMeter to implement data-driven testing using the CSV Data Set Config.
ALGORITHM
1. Start Apache JMeter (jmeter.bat or jmeter.sh) and rename the Test Plan.
2. Add a Thread Group under Test Plan.
3. Create users.csv with three lines containing username, password and expected message. Save it in the JMeter bin folder.
4. Set Number of Threads = 1 and Loop Count = 3.
5. Add Config Element → CSV Data Set Config and configure:
   - Filename: users.csv
   - Variable Names: username,password,expected
   - Delimiter: comma
   - Recycle on EOF: False
   - Stop thread on EOF: True
6. Add HTTP Cookie Manager and select Clear cookies each iteration.
7. Add HTTP Request POST /authenticate with parameters ${username} and ${password}.
8. Add Response Assertion with pattern ${expected}.
9. Add View Results Tree and Summary Report, run the plan and stop.
INPUT
File: users.csv
Line	Content
1	tomsmith,SuperSecretPassword!,You logged into a secure area!
2	tomsmith,wrongpass,Your password is invalid!
3	baduser,SuperSecretPassword!,Your username is invalid!

Test Plan Configuration
Element	Property	Value
Thread Group	Number of Threads	1
Thread Group	Ramp-up Period	1 second
Thread Group	Loop Count	3
CSV Data Set Config	Filename	users.csv
CSV Data Set Config	Variable Names	username,password,expected
CSV Data Set Config	Delimiter	,
CSV Data Set Config	Recycle on EOF / Stop thread on EOF	False / True
HTTP Cookie Manager	Clear cookies each iteration	Selected
HTTP Request	Method / Path	POST /authenticate
HTTP Request	Parameters	${username}, ${password}
Response Assertion	Pattern	${expected}

OUTPUT
Summary Report
Label	Samples	Error %
POST /authenticate	3	0.00%

View Results Tree: Three samples show the three data rows:
1. tomsmith / SuperSecretPassword!
2. tomsmith / wrongpass
3. baduser / SuperSecretPassword!
All three assertions pass.
RESULT
Thus, Apache JMeter was used to implement data-driven testing using the CSV Data Set Config and the results were verified.
